1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,884
A report only helps when somebody opens it.

2
00:00:03,884 --> 00:00:08,770
Report Subscriptions email a report on a schedule, to the people who need it.

3
00:00:08,770 --> 00:00:12,656
This video shows how to set one up, what the list tells you,

4
00:00:12,656 --> 00:00:16,070
and what happens on a site whose email is not ready.

5
00:00:20,670 --> 00:00:24,400
Nobody remembers to open the sales report every Monday.

6
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:26,724
A subscription does it for them:

7
00:00:26,724 --> 00:00:30,270
the report arrives in the inbox of whoever needs it.

8
00:00:31,020 --> 00:00:35,465
A subscription goes out every day for the day before, every week for

9
00:00:35,465 --> 00:00:39,370
the seven days before, or every month for the month before.

10
00:00:40,120 --> 00:00:45,127
The email shows the numbers and tables of the report, and can carry

11
00:00:45,127 --> 00:00:47,254
the report as a file too:

12
00:00:47,254 --> 00:00:48,900
CSV, Excel or PDF.

13
00:00:49,650 --> 00:00:52,056
The hour is in the site's time zone.

14
00:00:52,056 --> 00:00:56,869
A background task checks every few minutes for subscriptions that are due, and

15
00:00:56,869 --> 00:00:58,530
schedules the next one.

16
00:01:02,712 --> 00:01:08,182
Report Subscriptions is a feature under Tools, Features, in the Reporting category.

17
00:01:08,182 --> 00:01:09,350
Click Enable.

18
00:01:09,350 --> 00:01:14,452
It needs the Reports feature and the Email feature, and enables them with it.

19
00:01:27,948 --> 00:01:31,130
The Reports menu now has a Subscriptions item.

20
00:01:31,130 --> 00:01:35,474
Each report is still gated by its own permission, so a person can

21
00:01:35,474 --> 00:01:38,288
only subscribe to reports they may open.

22
00:01:39,870 --> 00:01:43,627
Who may manage subscriptions is a permission of its own:

23
00:01:43,627 --> 00:01:47,747
Manage report subscriptions, in the Reports section of a role.

24
00:01:47,747 --> 00:01:50,170
Administrators have it by default.

25
00:01:54,419 --> 00:01:58,597
A subscription can only be sent through an email provider.

26
00:01:58,597 --> 00:02:03,949
Under Settings, Email, this site says that no email provider is enabled yet.

27
00:02:04,402 --> 00:02:07,762
Back on the Features page, enable a provider.

28
00:02:07,762 --> 00:02:12,372
Here it is the SMTP provider, which sends through a mail server.

29
00:02:29,460 --> 00:02:33,690
The SMTP tab asks for the sender address, the host name and the

30
00:02:33,690 --> 00:02:37,308
port, and for credentials when the server needs them.

31
00:02:37,308 --> 00:02:41,354
This site has no mail server, so these values point nowhere.

32
00:02:41,354 --> 00:02:43,930
On your site, enter your own server.

33
00:02:48,143 --> 00:02:50,355
Open Reports, Subscriptions.

34
00:02:50,355 --> 00:02:51,916
The list is empty.

35
00:02:51,916 --> 00:02:53,803
Click Add subscription.

36
00:02:54,269 --> 00:02:59,144
Choose the Report, from every report you may open, listed by category.

37
00:02:59,144 --> 00:03:03,699
The Name is optional; the report's name is used when it is blank.

38
00:03:04,170 --> 00:03:08,150
Send chooses every day, every week or every month.

39
00:03:08,150 --> 00:03:12,840
For a weekly report, pick the Day of the week; for a monthly

40
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:16,109
one, the Day of the month, from 1 to 28.

41
00:03:16,109 --> 00:03:20,230
The Hour runs from 0 to 23, in the site's time zone.

42
00:03:20,696 --> 00:03:25,262
Under Email to, enter the addresses, separated by commas.

43
00:03:25,262 --> 00:03:28,088
Attach the report as adds a file:

44
00:03:28,088 --> 00:03:30,697
CSV, Excel or PDF, or No file.

45
00:03:30,697 --> 00:03:34,756
The email shows the numbers and tables either way.

46
00:03:35,211 --> 00:03:37,540
Leave On ticked, and click Save.

47
00:03:37,540 --> 00:03:42,626
The subscription's page opens, with a banner that says when it goes out next.

48
00:03:42,626 --> 00:03:48,631
Back in Report subscriptions, the list shows its schedule, its recipients and the next time.

49
00:03:52,863 --> 00:03:57,314
Save and send now saves the subscription and sends it straight away, for

50
00:03:57,314 --> 00:04:00,853
the period before, so you can check what recipients get.

51
00:04:01,309 --> 00:04:05,933
This site has no mail server, so the send fails, and the page says why:

52
00:04:05,933 --> 00:04:08,876
the report wasn't emailed, with the reason.

53
00:04:08,876 --> 00:04:12,539
A site with a working mail server sends the email here.

54
00:04:12,990 --> 00:04:16,583
The list shows the same thing on the subscription's row:

55
00:04:16,583 --> 00:04:19,654
Last run didn't go out, with the reason in red.

56
00:04:19,654 --> 00:04:23,769
Fix the cause, such as the email settings, and send it again with

57
00:04:23,769 --> 00:04:25,160
Save and send now.

58
00:04:29,453 --> 00:04:32,865
Untick On, and click Save, to pause a subscription.

59
00:04:32,865 --> 00:04:36,398
Back in the list it keeps an Off badge, and it is not

60
00:04:36,398 --> 00:04:38,673
sent until you turn it on again.

61
00:04:42,285 --> 00:04:45,042
Search finds a subscription by its name.

62
00:04:45,042 --> 00:04:50,135
Edit changes any setting, and Delete removes a subscription you no longer need.

63
00:04:54,335 --> 00:04:58,476
Subscriptions cover the reports under Reports that modules provide.

64
00:04:58,476 --> 00:05:02,445
Reports you build in the Report Builder cannot be subscribed to.

65
00:05:03,195 --> 00:05:05,899
To email one of those, use a workflow:

66
00:05:05,899 --> 00:05:10,262
when a report runs on a schedule, the Email Report task sends it.

67
00:05:10,262 --> 00:05:13,395
The Report Builder workflows video shows how.

68
00:05:17,595 --> 00:05:19,743
A weekly service review:

69
00:05:19,743 --> 00:05:25,325
Queue service level every Monday at seven, to the supervisors, as a PDF.

70
00:05:26,075 --> 00:05:27,796
A monthly bill check:

71
00:05:27,796 --> 00:05:33,275
Queue usage for billing on the first of the month, to finance, as an Excel file.

72
00:05:34,025 --> 00:05:35,265
A daily pulse:

73
00:05:35,265 --> 00:05:39,853
Call insights each morning for the day before, to the manager of the

74
00:05:39,853 --> 00:05:41,465
floor, with no file.

75
00:05:43,465 --> 00:05:47,564
Report subscriptions put the right report in the right inbox on time.

76
00:05:47,564 --> 00:05:48,985
Thanks for watching.

